---
export const prerender = true;

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ServiceLayout from '../../components/service/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { serviceBySlug } from '../../config/services';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site';

const service = serviceBySlug('ai-agent-audit')!;
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What does an AI agent audit cover?',
    a: 'Four things: cost (model, token and API spend per task), reliability (how often runs fail, loop or give wrong answers), risk (prompt injection, data exposure, over-broad permissions) and fit (whether each step needs AI at all). You get a prioritised list of fixes with the expected effect of each.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which tools and platforms can you audit?',
    a: 'Agents and automations built in n8n, Make, Zapier, Vapi, Retell, custom code calling OpenAI, Anthropic or Gemini APIs, and website chatbots. If it runs on prompts, tools and logs, it can usually be reviewed.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can an audit reduce AI costs?',
    a: 'Common savings come from using a smaller model for simple steps, trimming oversized prompts and context, caching repeated calls, stopping retry loops, and replacing AI steps that plain rules handle just as well. The audit estimates spend per run before and after so you can see the difference.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What access do you need?',
    a: 'Read access to the workflows or code, recent run logs, and billing or usage pages for the AI providers. Production write access is not needed for the audit itself.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will you fix the problems too?',
    a: 'Yes, if you want. The audit ends with a fixed-price quote for the top fixes. Many are small: a model swap, a guardrail, a tighter prompt, a permission removed.',
  },
];

const checks = [
  { k: 'Cost', d: 'Spend per run and per month, by model and step. Where tokens are wasted.' },
  { k: 'Reliability', d: 'Failure, retry and loop rates. Where outputs go wrong and nobody notices.' },
  { k: 'Security', d: 'Prompt injection paths, leaked keys, data sent to models, tool permissions.' },
  { k: 'Fit', d: 'Steps that do not need AI at all, and steps that need a human checkpoint.' },
];

const pageLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: service.title,
    description: service.metaDescription,
    url: `${SITE.url}${service.path}`,
    provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name, url: SITE.url },
    areaServed: 'Worldwide',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: 499, priceCurrency: 'USD', url: `${SITE.url}${service.path}` },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Services', item: `${SITE.url}/services/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: service.navTitle, item: `${SITE.url}${service.path}` },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
    })),
  },
];
---

<Base title={service.metaTitle} description={service.metaDescription} canonicalPath={service.path} jsonLd={pageLd}>
  <ServiceLayout
    service={service}
    lede="You already run AI agents, chatbots or n8n automations. This audit shows what they really cost, where they fail quietly, what they expose, and the fixes that make them cheaper and safer."
    artAlt="Abstract glass panels with flowing data lines on a warm studio table"
    faqs={faqs}
    visualTone="tone-cream"
    problemTitle="AI that works in the demo and leaks in production"
    problemLead="Agents get shipped fast. Months later the bill has grown, some runs fail silently, and nobody is sure what data goes where."
    deliverablesTitle="What the audit produces"
    deliverablesLead="A clear picture of every agent and workflow, plus a fix list ordered by money saved and risk removed."
    processTitle="How the audit runs"
    processVariant="timeline"
    scopeTitle="What the audit includes (and the honest limits)"
  >
    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div class="aa-card" data-reveal>
        <div class="aa-top">
          <span class="aa-title">Audit scorecard · example layout</span>
          <span class="aa-tag">Illustrative</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="aa-grid">
          {
            checks.map((c, i) => (
              <li class="aa-item">
                <span class="aa-num">0{i + 1}</span>
                <h3>{c.k}</h3>
                <p>{c.d}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="aa-foot">Every finding gets a severity, an estimated effect and a fixed-price fix option.</p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="problem">
      <p>
        Most AI systems are built quickly to prove they work. That is the right call at the
        start. The problems appear later: a large model handling a task a small one could do,
        prompts that grew to thousands of tokens, a retry loop that runs all night, a chatbot that
        can be talked into ignoring its instructions.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>None of this shows up in a demo. It shows up in the invoice and in the support
        inbox.</strong> An audit looks at the real runs, the real logs and the real bill, then
        separates what needs fixing from what is fine.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Typical quick wins:</strong> swapping to a smaller model for classification
        steps, trimming context, caching repeated calls, adding a confidence check before an
        agent acts, and removing permissions the agent never needed.
      </div>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="deliverables">
      <ul class="deliver-grid">
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>System inventory</h3>
            <p>Every agent, workflow, model, tool and data source, mapped in one place.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Cost breakdown</h3>
            <p>Spend per run and per month by model and step, with the waste highlighted.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Reliability report</h3>
            <p>Failure, retry and wrong-output patterns from your real logs.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Risk review</h3>
            <p>Prompt injection paths, data exposure, key handling and over-broad tool access.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Prioritised fix list</h3>
            <p>Each fix ranked by money saved and risk removed, with effort estimates.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="deliver-item">
          <span class="di-num">06</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Fixed-price fix quote</h3>
            <p>Optional: the top fixes implemented for a fixed price, so the audit turns into results.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="process">
      <ol class="p-timeline">
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 01</span>
          <h3>Share read access</h3>
          <p>Workflows or code, recent run logs and AI provider usage pages. No production write access needed.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 02</span>
          <h3>Map and measure</h3>
          <p>Every agent and step is mapped, then cost and failure rates are measured from real runs.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 03</span>
          <h3>Test the edges</h3>
          <p>Prompts and tools are checked against injection, bad inputs and data leaks in a safe copy.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="p-num">STEP 04</span>
          <h3>Report and quote</h3>
          <p>You get the scorecard, the fix list and a fixed price for the fixes worth doing.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="scope">
      <ul>
        <li>Covers agents, chatbots and automations in n8n, Make, Zapier, Vapi, Retell and custom code using major AI APIs.</li>
        <li>Cost figures come from your real usage data; estimates of savings are labelled as estimates.</li>
        <li>Security checks are practical reviews, not a formal penetration test or compliance certification.</li>
        <li>Fixes are optional and quoted separately at a fixed price.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The scorecard above shows the layout of the report, not results from a real client.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </ServiceLayout>
</Base>

<style>
  .aa-card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .aa-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .aa-tag {
    color: var(--color-ink-3);
  }

  .aa-grid {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .aa-item {
    padding: 1.4rem 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .aa-item + .aa-item {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .aa-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-indigo);
  }

  .aa-item h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }

  .aa-item p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }

  .aa-foot {
    padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .aa-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }

    .aa-item:nth-child(3) {
      border-left: 0;
    }

    .aa-item:nth-child(n + 3) {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 32rem) {
    .aa-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .aa-item + .aa-item {
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    }
  }
</style>
